EXPORT_OPTIONS_TITLE=Export URDF
EXPORT_KEEP_UNSUPPORTED=Keep the elements this editor has no field for (transmissions, gazebo, joint dynamics...)
EXPORT_KEEP_UNSUPPORTED_HINT=Off by default: they are left out of the file, as before. When on, they are written back as the source file had them, except those that name a joint or link that was deleted.
EXPORT_UNSUPPORTED_COUNT=The source file has {count} element(s) this editor does not keep.
EXPORT_UNSUPPORTED_NONE=Nothing in the source file is left out of the export.
EXPORT_Y_UP=Write the model for a Y-up scene (Three.js)
EXPORT_Y_UP_HINT=Off by default: the file keeps the Z-up convention of URDF. When on, a root link turns the world so that Y points up, as in the STUDIO scene; the scale is y_up_scale in the configuration file (1 by default).
PHYS_LINE=[{rule}] {what} - {element}: {value} (limit: {limit}). Suggestion: {fix}
PHYS_NONE=No physical issues found.
PHYS_SUMMARY={count} physical warning(s) in {file}
PHYS_ERROR=Cannot read the model: {error}
PHYS_USAGE=Usage: main.py --cli physical-check FILE.urdf [--json] [--mesh-root DIR]  (exit 0: none, 1: warnings, 2: error)
PHYS_R_tree_no_root=No root link (every link has a parent)
PHYS_F_tree_no_root=Remove the joint that closes the loop, or leave one link without a parent
PHYS_R_tree_multiple_roots=More than one root link
PHYS_F_tree_multiple_roots=Join the extra roots to the tree with a joint, or remove them
PHYS_R_tree_cycle=The joints form a cycle
PHYS_F_tree_cycle=Remove one joint of the loop: a URDF is a tree
PHYS_R_tree_orphan_link=Link not used by any joint
PHYS_F_tree_orphan_link=Join '{fix}' to the tree with a joint, or delete the link
PHYS_R_tree_unreachable_link=Link out of reach of the root
PHYS_F_tree_unreachable_link=Join it to the chain that starts at '{fix}'
PHYS_R_tree_multiple_parents=Link with more than one parent
PHYS_F_tree_multiple_parents=Keep one parent joint and remove the others
PHYS_R_tree_unknown_link=Joint names a link that does not exist
PHYS_F_tree_unknown_link=Add the link or correct the name in the joint
PHYS_R_duplicate_name=Name used more than once
PHYS_F_duplicate_name=Rename the duplicates so that '{fix}' is unique
PHYS_R_mass_not_positive=Mass is not above 0
PHYS_F_mass_not_positive=Set a mass above 0 (for example {fix} kg) or remove the inertial
PHYS_R_inertia_not_finite=The inertia has a value that is not a number
PHYS_F_inertia_not_finite=Replace it with finite numbers
PHYS_R_inertia_not_positive_definite=The inertia tensor is not positive definite
PHYS_F_inertia_not_positive_definite=Add {fix} to ixx, iyy and izz, or enter the real tensor
PHYS_R_inertia_triangle=The principal moments break the triangle inequality
PHYS_F_inertia_triangle=Raise the smallest principal moment by {fix}, or enter the real tensor
PHYS_R_limit_missing=Joint without a limit
PHYS_F_limit_missing=Add a limit with lower, upper, effort and velocity
PHYS_R_limit_inverted=Lower limit above the upper limit
PHYS_F_limit_inverted=Swap them ({fix})
PHYS_R_velocity_not_positive=Velocity limit is not above 0
PHYS_F_velocity_not_positive=Set a velocity above 0 (for example {fix})
PHYS_R_effort_not_positive=Effort limit is not above 0
PHYS_F_effort_not_positive=Set an effort above 0 (for example {fix})
PHYS_R_continuous_with_limits=Continuous joint with lower and upper limits
PHYS_F_continuous_with_limits=Remove lower and upper, or make the joint revolute
PHYS_R_axis_zero=The joint axis is zero
PHYS_F_axis_zero=Give it a direction, for example {fix}
PHYS_R_axis_not_unit=The joint axis is not of length 1
PHYS_F_axis_not_unit=Normalise it to {fix}
PHYS_R_mesh_missing=Mesh file not found
PHYS_F_mesh_missing=Fix the path or add the file
PHYS_R_mesh_scale_invalid=The mesh scale is not reasonable
PHYS_F_mesh_scale_invalid=Use a scale such as {fix}, or the real unit of the mesh
PHYS_R_mesh_scale_anisotropic=The mesh scale differs between axes
PHYS_F_mesh_scale_anisotropic=Use {fix} on the three axes unless the stretch is intended
PHYS_R_units_length=The length looks like millimetres
PHYS_F_units_length=If it is in millimetres, use {fix} m
PHYS_R_units_angle=The angle looks like degrees
PHYS_F_units_angle=If it is in degrees, use {fix} rad
PHYS_R_units_mass=The mass looks like grams
PHYS_F_units_mass=If it is in grams, use {fix} kg
